    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 120 ft., Keen Smell",
    "tactics": "Swamp Cats hunt in pairs or small groups, using the terrain to stalk prey before committing to Pounce. Pack ### Tactics and Pounce together make their opening turn devastating — one cat charges to trigger Prone while the second ### Attacks with subtracted dice against the downed target. They break off if badly wounded, retreating into the swamp to recover.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Bite [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 7 + Melee Combat 4), Reach 5 ft.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 14 damage (9 + 5 Str).</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 14 damage, DR halved (round up).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Claw [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 7 + Melee Combat 4), Reach 5 ft.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 14 damage (9 + 5 Str).</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 14 damage, DR halved (round up).</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Keen Smell: Scent-based Perception checks have Fortune. Pack ### Tactics: When an ally is within 5 feet of the target, subtract 1 from both attack dice. Pounce: If the Swamp Cat moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits with a claw attack on the same turn, the target must make a Fortitude save, opposed by the Cat's Str 5 + Melee Combat 5). On failure, the target gains the Prone condition. If the target is Prone, the Swamp Cat may immediately make one bite attack against it as a [Free] action.</p>",
